      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "The Islamic Scholarship Fund demonstrates a consistent track record of professional placement for its scholars. Since 2009, they have distributed <cite id=\"12\">672 total awards</cite> to help Muslims enter fields like journalism and law. Their financial management is characterized by <cite id=\"13\">100% independent board members</cite> and a <cite id=\"14\">Platinum Seal of Transparency</cite> from Candid. Furthermore, the organization has achieved a <cite id=\"15\">36.5% three-year revenue growth rate</cite>, suggesting increasing donor trust and expanding program capacity."
      ],
      "summary": "founded in 2009, the Islamic Scholarship Fund (ISF) works to increase American Muslim representation in media, law, and public policy. The organization addresses the lack of Muslim voices in influential fields by providing <cite id=\"1\">scholarships, film grants, and internships</cite>. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"2\">total revenue of $1,922,887</cite>, marking a significant increase from previous years. ISF has awarded <cite id=\"3\">$3.67 million in total funds</cite> since its inception, supporting <cite id=\"4\">692 beneficiaries</cite> to date. Their model focuses on capacity building, helping students secure <cite id=\"5\">congressional policy fellowships and judicial internships</cite>. Data from 2024 indicates a high success rate, with <cite id=\"6\">88% of alumni working in their chosen fields</cite> and a <cite id=\"7\">100% graduation rate</cite> among supported students. While the organization maintains a <cite id=\"8\">91.67/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>, it operates with a balanced profile of strengths and structural gaps. The charity is <cite id=\"9\">zakat-eligible</cite>, specifically serving the categories of the poor, the needy, and those in the way of Allah.",
